## ✅ Phase 2: System Design & Distributed Architecture (Months 4–6)

### 🎯 Key Goals:
- Learn how to build scalable and resilient systems
- Gain expertise in microservices architecture and design
Understand microservices deeply
Build a mental framework for architecture tradeoffs


### 🔧 Skills to Master:
- **Low-Level Design (LLD)**: OOP modeling, use cases,Object-oriented design, Class relationships, Use Case modeling
- **High-Level Design (HLD)**: Component, Sequence, Deployment diagrams,UML Diagrams, Component diagrams, Sequence diagrams
- **Microservices Patterns**: API Gateway, Circuit Breaker, Service Registry, SAGA
- **Data & Communication**: REST vs gRPC, Kafka, RabbitMQ, Asynchronous Messaging
- **Resilience Patterns**: Retry, Timeout, Rate Limiting, Idempotency
Architecture Styles: Microservices, Event-driven, Layered, Serverless

Key Concepts: CAP Theorem, Eventual Consistency, Idempotency, Rate Limiting, Throttling

Resilience & Observability: Circuit Breakers, Retries, Timeouts (using Resilience4j/Spring Cloud)

Communication:

  REST vs gRPC

  Async with Kafka, RabbitMQ

  API Versioning, OpenAPI/Swagger

### 📚 Tools & Frameworks:
- Spring Boot, Spring Cloud, Kafka, RabbitMQ, Swagger, Resilience4j

